## Problem classes

### `Vpn overlay classified as Other`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| AUTO flaps PROXY↔VPN when VPN is up | `activeNetwork` is `TRANSPORT_VPN` | Strip our VPN; classify underlying Wi-Fi/cell/other |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Split-brain node`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Same node ID, two paths; VPN stuck `REQUESTING_CONFIGURATION` while PROXY "works" | libzt and JNI both opened `identity.secret` — usually an **in-flight start** the stop check missed (`isRunning` flips after `start()` returns) | Synchronous start tokens (`startCounter`/`stoppedToken`); treat `isRunning \|\| startRequested` as active so STOP is always sent; superseded starts self-abort; never two live nodes |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Slow stop breaks the swap`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Swap only fails while networks are still joining; STOP takes minutes | Start coroutine holds the service mutex through long joins (120s `waitForNetworkReady` each); STOP queues behind it, `stopAndAwait` times out, apply proceeds → split-brain | Abort predicate in every wait loop (checked ~100ms); bounded per-item timeouts; readiness also arrives via the event listener, so short waits lose nothing |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `onDestroy cancels its own cleanup`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Stale system HTTP_PROXY / zombie libzt node after service death | `onDestroy` launched cleanup on `scope` then immediately `serviceJob.cancel()` — coroutine cancelled before dispatch | Final cleanup on a detached scope (`CoroutineScope(SupervisorJob() + Dispatchers.IO)`), then cancel the service job |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `FGS 5s rule on early returns`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `ForegroundServiceDidNotStartInTimeException` when a start is refused or superseded | `startForegroundService()` was answered with `startForeground()` only inside a coroutine that early-returned | Call `startForeground()` synchronously in `onStartCommand` before any async branch; early-exit paths `stopForeground(REMOVE)` + `stopSelf()` |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `HTTP_PROXY survives PROXY→VPN swap`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Global still loopback after VPN up | Stopped proxy before `disable()` | `SystemProxyManager.disable()` then `ProxyModeService.stopAndAwait()` |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Stack swap races`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Orchestrator starts JNI while libzt still up | Service `shutdown()` has no completion callback; a stop timeout was logged and apply proceeded anyway | Companion `stopAndAwait()` returns Boolean (15s); on timeout **abort the swap** (throw, leave `lastApplied` stale); wait until the vacated UDP port (9993/9994) is bindable before starting the other stack |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Equal plan re-swap`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| AUTO WiFi A PROXY → WiFi B PROXY triggers stack churn | Re-applied identical `RuntimePlan` | Skip only when `plan == lastApplied` **and** live stack state matches (`runtimeMatches`) — a crashed/refused service must re-apply on the next refresh (self-healing), not no-op |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `VPN mode leaves HTTP_PROXY loopback`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `apply_mode VPN` but `http_proxy` still `127.0.0.1:*`; logcat empty | No consent dialog — resolver fell back to PROXY silently; orchestrator logs were `Log.d` | `apply_mode VPN` must `VpnService.prepare()` from Activity first; `applyVpn` always calls `SystemProxyManager.disable()` even when proxy service already dead; use `Log.i` on apply |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `ADB extras dropped on running MainActivity`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `am start` PROXY works, later VPN/stop_all no-op; "Activity not started, intent has been delivered" | `launchMode=standard` + launcher `MAIN` — OEM delivers to top instance without `onNewIntent` | `singleTop` + action `com.brukb.zerotier.DEBUG`; consume extras after handle. ADB: `am start -a com.brukb.zerotier.DEBUG -n …/.ui.MainActivity -f 0x20000000 --es …` |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Consent fallback still carries vpnNetworkId`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| UI/services act on VPN id while runtime is PROXY | Consent path set `vpnNetworkId` before downgrade | Set `vpnNetworkId` only when `runtime == VPN` |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `VPN main net change while VPN up`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Pin Main / route change while VPN running — old net still on TUN | `applyVpn` only starts when `!isRunning`; equal-runtime refresh skips swap | If VPN running and `plan.vpnNetworkId != lastApplied?.vpnNetworkId`, `stopVpnLocked()` then start new id |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Shizuku grant does not enable HTTP_PROXY`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Grant succeeds but apps still bypass proxy | `plan == lastApplied` skips re-apply | After grant: `invalidateAppliedPlan()` then `refresh()`; run Shizuku `waitFor` off main thread |

